Spec: Schema

ID:
  @subtask

Purpose:
  Schema for SUBTASK — the smallest execution unit (MODUL -> CASE ->
  TASK -> SUBTASK). A subtask record is a mini execution contract:
  one goal, bounded scope, explicit forbidden list, dependency edges,
  its own lifecycle state, and a done-proof.

Owns: schemas/subtask.sdd

Schema:

  id: SUBTASK-<TASK-ID>-<NN>
      example: SUBTASK-TASK-001-03 (third unit of TASK-001)

  parent: TASK-<id>
      The owning task (bax ../tasks/TASK-STATE-MACHINE.sdd). A
      subtask NEVER exists without a parent task.

  goal: <one line>
      Single primary objective. If the goal needs "and", it is
      likely two subtasks.

  scope:
    allowed:
      - <paths or scopes the unit may touch>
    allowed_actions:
      - code | tests | docs | config | refactor | research
    forbidden:
      - <explicit prohibitions beyond allowed>

  depends_on:
    - SUBTASK-<id>
      Units of the SAME task that must be DONE before this one.
      Cross-task dependencies live on the task, not the subtask.

  state: <SUBTASK-STATE-MACHINE state>
      bax ../tasks/SUBTASK-STATE-MACHINE.sdd (TODO -> ... -> DONE).

  done_proof:
    artifact: <file(s) or record(s) produced>
    validation: <how correctness was proven — test run, review id,
                 scan id; NEVER "looks correct">

Rules:

  [SB1] id MUST be unique and stable across the task lifetime.
  [SB2] goal MUST be a single objective — split otherwise.
  [SB3] forbidden list MUST be explicit — empty forbidden requires
        an explicit "forbidden: none (scoped to allowed only)" entry.
  [SB4] state transitions MUST follow SUBTASK-STATE-MACHINE — no
        direct TODO -> DONE.
  [SB5] done_proof MUST exist BEFORE state moves to DONE (bax
        ../tasks/DONE-PROOF.sdd).
  [SB6] A parent task is complete ONLY when ALL its subtasks are
        DONE (feeds task_complete check in commands/sdd-next.sdd).
  [SB7] New dependencies introduced by a unit MUST pass
        ../../gates/dependency-gate.sdd BEFORE implementation —
        never added mid-unit without APPROVE.

Templates:
  Instance files live in projects/{project_name}/tasks/ alongside
  their parent task records; creation uses this schema directly.

Navigation:
  SubtaskStateMachine: @../tasks/SUBTASK-STATE-MACHINE.sdd
  ExecutionContract: @../tasks/EXECUTION-CONTRACT.sdd
  TaskSchema: @task.sdd
  DependencyGate: @../gates/dependency-gate.sdd
  DownUpTransition: @../branches/DOWN-UP-TRANSITION.sdd

State: +
  (Phase 155: created as the unit-level contract for /sdd-next
   --subtask resolution; a trimmed per-unit instance of the
   EXECUTION-CONTRACT discipline)
